From: Bren Marshall <brenallenmarshall@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 16:23:20 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] perf(ui): build the stock eye on a worker thread at start

StockEye::new compiles the composite and trace shaders on the UI thread
before the first frame: about 450 ms on a Windows DX12 adapter, with the
window already shown and not answering. Build it on its own thread and
take it on a later frame, as the browser shell already does. Until it
lands, the viewport draws the stock sheet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
